//
// HZM coop [user 2026-09-05] m3l1a THE PLAYER'S TRANSMISSION.  Two retail Omaha dialogue wavs
// re-declared under coop_* names so the exchange carries further up the beach than the retail 1500.
// SAME PATH AS THE RETAIL PARENTS, DELIBERATELY: `dialog streamed`. S_OPENAL_StartSound diverts a
// streamed alias to the 2D path BEFORE the 3D start gate (snd_openal_new.cpp:2083), so there is no
// maxDist cut-off at all - the 2D branch fades LINEARLY from minDist to maxDist (:3305-3310) and
// pans by entity position. That path honours the alias volume, rides the Dialogue slider and OWNS
// the vox sidechain. The first draft of these lines was `voice loaded`, the 3D path, where the
// alias volume is discarded by set_3d (bug-2452), the line rides the SFX bus and is ducked x0.65
// under every German bark - quieter than the radioman it replaced, on the wrong slider.
// 3000, NOT 9000: on a linear fade 9000 is near-full volume across the whole map with only pan for
// position; 3000 is audible along the beach and gone at the bluff.
// SAFE TO RE-ALIAS BECAUSE NOTHING SAYS THESE - the standing rule (`say` resolves the lipsync anim
// BY ALIAS NAME) applies to `say` only; these are played with playsound off the radio set. The
// retail aliases streamed_dfr_scripted_M3L1_036h / _045a are untouched and still used by the
// hush-off path. Confirm in the log with the VOXSTART line (chan=dialog) when the set is used.
// LENGTHS, MEASURED, because the beat's waits are spelled out in seconds: 036h 5.841s, 045a 4.506s
// (22050Hz mono, from the shipped wavs).
alias coop_radio_m3l1_036h sound/dialogue/m3l1/A/dfr_scripted_M3L1_036h.wav soundparms 1.5 0.0 1.0 0.0 200 3000 dialog streamed maps "m e t"	//5.841s
alias coop_radio_m3l1_045a sound/dialogue/m3l1/A/dfr_scripted_M3L1_045a.wav soundparms 1.5 0.0 1.0 0.0 200 3000 dialog streamed maps "m e t"	//4.506s
aliascache coop_radio_static_loop sound/coop_fx/radio_static_loop.wav soundparms 1.0 0.0 1.0 0.0 200 2000 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"

// HZM coop - DISTANCE GUNFIRE TAILS: additive report layered on far-away shots by the cgame
// bullet-volley hook (coop_gunTail). Mid = crack-slap (played 1400-2800u), far = rolling
// rumble-echo (2800u+). Big distances so they carry across the map.
aliascache snd_gun_tail_mid1 sound/coop_fx/gun_tail_mid1.wav soundparms 1.3 0.1 1.0 0.05 1000 6000 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
aliascache snd_gun_tail_mid2 sound/coop_fx/gun_tail_mid2.wav soundparms 1.3 0.1 1.0 0.05 1000 6000 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
aliascache snd_gun_tail_far1 sound/coop_fx/gun_tail_far1.wav soundparms 1.5 0.1 0.95 0.05 1600 10000 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
aliascache snd_gun_tail_far2 sound/coop_fx/gun_tail_far2.wav soundparms 1.5 0.1 0.95 0.05 1600 10000 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"

// [user 2026-08-28] GUN SUB LAYER: the low-frequency half of a gunshot, which the retail aliases do
// not carry at all. Derived from the fire sounds already in this mod (transient -> 190 Hz low-pass ->
// pitch down -> fast attack, exponential decay), so the low end matches the guns actually in game.
// Tiered by weapon class and scaled by the same heft value that drives recoil, droop and movement, so
// a Panzerschreck lands in the chest and a Luger barely registers. Volumes are modest because this
// layers UNDER the existing fire alias - it is felt, not heard.
aliascache snd_gun_sub_light   sound/coop_fx/gun_sub_light.wav   soundparms 0.75 0.05 1.0 0.04  600 2600 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
aliascache snd_gun_sub_mid     sound/coop_fx/gun_sub_mid.wav     soundparms 0.95 0.06 1.0 0.04  800 3600 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
aliascache snd_gun_sub_heavy   sound/coop_fx/gun_sub_heavy.wav   soundparms 1.15 0.06 1.0 0.03 1000 4800 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
aliascache snd_gun_sub_massive sound/coop_fx/gun_sub_massive.wav soundparms 1.35 0.07 1.0 0.03 1200 6500 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"

// [user 2026-08-09] THE SORTIE (m2l2b finale) - the U-boat engine set retail recorded for the sub
// pens (SubPen_Sub_Start/Moving) and then scoped ONLY to MP "dm obj" maps, so the campaign never
// heard it once. Re-aliased for m/e/t with cinema-range distances: she sails up to ~10,000u from
// the players' ears and the stock 5,000u falloff would mute her mid-crossing. The horn is the
// mod's own shipped distant_horn.mp3 - a far-off harbor horn, exactly right in a blizzard.
aliascache coop_sub_start  sound/vehicle/SubPen_Sub_Start.wav  soundparms 2.0 0.0 1.0 0.0 2000 18000 auto loaded maps "m e t"
aliascache coop_sub_moving sound/vehicle/SubPen_Sub_Moving.wav soundparms 2.0 0.0 1.0 0.0 2000 18000 auto loaded maps "m e t"
// [user 2026-08-09] distant_horn.mp3 never SHIPPED - the alias pointed at nothing, hence the
// silent horn. This wav is synthesized (layered low sines + tremolo + lowpass) and ships with
// the mod. COMMENT ON ITS OWN LINE: a trailing comment on an alias line can kill the parse
// silently (the working sub_start/sub_moving lines end clean at the maps spec).
aliascache coop_sub_horn sound/coop_amb/uboat_horn.wav soundparms 1.2 0.0 1.0 0.0 2000 20000 auto loaded maps "m e t"

//[user 2026-08-10] blueprint pickup. Retail ships three paper-pickup wavs but aliases them
//only for t3l1 (pickup_combination / pickup_portfolio), so they are unreachable on every other
//map. Same asset, our own alias, full map coverage.
//ALL MAPS: bLoadForMap (scriptmaster.cpp:417) prefix-matches each token against mapname, so
//"m e t dm obj train" covers retail but misses every custom map. The "always" token sets
//bAlwaysLoaded and registers the alias BEFORE the map filter is consulted at all.
//aliascache, not alias: EV_RegisterAliasAndCache PRECACHES the sample. With a plain alias the
//wav loads on first play and the client hitches at the pickup - measured 2026-08-10, the server
//frame graph was flat at worst=26ms straight through BP PICKUP, so the stall was never server-side.
aliascache coop_bp_pickup sound/items/Item_PaperPU_01.wav soundparms 1.2 0.0 1.0 0.0 100 2000 item loaded always maps "m e t dm obj train"

//
// PHASE C - the investigator's alarm shout [user 2026-08-10]: "when the guard that is standing over
// the body does end up escalating to have him yell 'Alarm Alarm' in german (distance based)".
// RETAIL AUDIO, not invented: these are the two real German alarm lines, DENGM_E1L4_GS8607
// ("Alarm! Alarm!") and DENGM_E1L4_GO8307 ("Intruder! Alarm!"), found by searching the shipped
// uberdialog for a subtitle that actually says Alarm - only three lines in the whole game do.
// RE-DECLARED HERE under new names because the retail aliases are scoped `maps "e1l4 "` and would
// therefore never load on m2l2a (docs/reference/tiki_and_sound_aliases.md: an alias whose map spec
// does not cover the level silently never loads). Same wav, same soundparms, wider scope.
// `alias` and NOT `aliascache`: these are `streamed`, and aliascache on a streamed alias forces it
// resident and defeats the streaming (bug-1672). soundparms 160/2100 is the retail falloff, which is
// what makes it distance-based as asked.
// forcesubtitle DROPPED: with it the engine logged "Unknown parameter for coop_alarm_yell alias" and
// the alias was rejected outright - the same fragile subtitle token bug-1672 warns about. The SHOUT
// is the requirement, the caption was not, so it goes rather than risk the line not registering.
alias coop_alarm_yell sound/dialogue/Mission_1/Axis/DENGM_E1L4_GS8607xc01.mp3 soundparms 1.5 0 1 0 160 2100 dialog streamed maps "m e t dm obj train"
alias coop_alarm_yell2 sound/dialogue/Mission_1/Axis/DENGM_E1L4_GO8307xk02.mp3 soundparms 1.5 0 1 0 160 2100 dialog streamed maps "m e t dm obj train"

// [user 2026-08-11] RADIO DISTRACTION (m6l1c storage room). Coop-owned copies of three retail
// sounds, because every retail alias for them is map-scoped to OTHER levels and would silently
// fail to resolve here: radio_loop is maps "m2l1 m6l2a train", radio_on is "e3l4 obj", radio_off
// is "obj". Same files, same falloff intent, full coop map spec.
// Mec_RadioMusic_01.wav is the only actual music track (~4 min) and lives LOOSE in
// main/sound/mechanics - it is in no pk3. streamed + alias (never aliascache) because of its size.
// 150 -> 800 is the distance falloff: audible across the storage room, gone from the corridor.
alias coop_radio_music sound/mechanics/Mec_RadioMusic_01.wav soundparms 0.75 0.0 1.0 0.0 300 1200 local streamed maps "m e t dm obj train"
alias coop_radio_on sound/coop_fx/radio_static1.wav soundparms 1.0 0.1 1.0 0.0 150 900 item loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
alias coop_radio_off sound/coop_fx/radio_static1.wav soundparms 1.0 0.1 1.0 0.0 150 900 item loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"

// [user 2026-08-12] FALSE ORDERS - the reply from the receiving station, not the player.
// The den_ PREFIX IS LOAD-BEARING. cg_commands.cpp:3883 shows an alias's subtitle when
// g_subtitle is set OR the alias name starts with "den" - which is how vanilla German
// dialogue is subtitled for everyone regardless of settings. Renaming these coop_* would
// silently drop the subtitles for any player who has not turned subtitles on.
// The engine then draws them itself (cl_uiview3d.cpp:732): facfont-20, URed, bottom of screen,
// auto-wrapped, on screen for 2500*((len/68)+1)+1500 ms. Nothing is drawn by our HUD code, so
// these look exactly like every other German line in the game.
// Three aliases rather than one long string: that is how retail does multi-line dialogue, and
// it means each line appears as it is spoken instead of a wall of text arriving at once.
alias den_coop_falseorder1 sound/coop_vo/den_coop_falseorder1.wav soundparms 2.6 0.0 1.0 0.0 900 2600 dialog streamed subtitle "This is Sector North. Receipt confirmed, Eagle." maps "m e t dm obj"
alias den_coop_falseorder2 sound/coop_vo/den_coop_falseorder2.wav soundparms 2.6 0.0 1.0 0.0 900 2600 dialog streamed subtitle "Authorization Habicht verified. Message being forwarded." maps "m e t dm obj"
alias den_coop_falseorder3 sound/coop_vo/den_coop_falseorder3.wav soundparms 2.6 0.0 1.0 0.0 900 2600 dialog streamed subtitle "All reserves are being redeployed north. Out." maps "m e t dm obj"

// The unstable carrier the voice sits on: MOHAA's own Mec_RadioLoop_03/04/05 - the Omaha bunker
// set (m3l1b:376 plays loop_04 on $bunker_radio) - concatenated in a shuffled, non-repeating
// order and crossfaded end-to-start so it loops without a seam. A COPY rather than a reference:
// the retail m3l1b_radio2 alias is scoped maps "m3l1b " and would fail silently anywhere else.
// Volume 0.16 is the mix the user picked (bed 16 dB under the voice); tune it HERE, not at the
// call site, so there is one number to change.
aliascache coop_radio_bed sound/coop_fx/coop_radio_bed.wav soundparms 0.16 0.0 1.0 0.0 200 1200 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"

//[user 2026-08-13, bug-1783] THE STEALTH PICKUP SOUNDS WERE SILENT ON m6l2a, and the log said so:
//"ERROR: Entity::Sound: pickup_papers needs an alias" / "pickup_uniform needs an alias". Two
//different causes, one symptom:
//  * pickup_uniform EXISTS but is scoped maps "m2l2a m4l3 m6l1c" and "e1l4 e3l1" - m6l2a is in
//    neither, and an alias whose map spec does not cover the level silently never loads.
//  * pickup_papers does not exist at all. Only pickup_papers1 does, and it is likewise scoped
//    without m6l2a.
//Re-declared here under the SAME names with a wider scope rather than editing the retail-shaped
//aliases in ubersound.scr, which is the pattern this file already uses for the alarm-shout lines:
//same wav, same soundparms, scope that actually covers where it is called.
aliascache pickup_papers sound/items/Item_PaperPU_01.wav soundparms 1.5 0.0 1.0 0.0 100 2000 item loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
aliascache pickup_uniform sound/items/Item_UniformPU_03.wav soundparms 1.2 0.0 1.0 0.0 100 2000 item loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"

// [user 2026-08-28] LONG-RANGE SHELL WHISTLE for the Omaha beach.
// arty_leadin2..7 carry maxdist 1600, and in this engine that is a HARD START GATE, not a rolloff:
// S_OPENAL_ShouldStart (snd_openal_new.cpp:1615) returns Square(maxDist) > distSquared and it gates
// pChannel->play() outright. So past 1600 units the incoming whistle does not merely fade - it never
// plays. On a beach thousands of units deep that means shells arrive as a bare, contextless thump with
// no warning, which is most of why the shelling reads as background noise instead of danger.
//
// 900/16000 is the shape retail already ships for long-range leadins (arty_leadin08/09, m5l3), so it
// is a proven parameter set. CHANNEL IS 'auto', NOT 'local': local means CHAN_LOCAL, 2D and
// non-positional, which would play every shell at full volume in all four players' heads regardless of
// where it landed - the same defect the headshot cue had.
aliascache coop_arty_leadin_far1 sound/weapons/explo/Exp_LeadIn_07.wav soundparms 0.8 0.2 0.7 0.5 900 16000 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
aliascache coop_arty_leadin_far2 sound/weapons/explo/Exp_LeadIn_08.wav soundparms 0.8 0.2 0.7 0.5 900 16000 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
aliascache coop_arty_leadin_far3 sound/weapons/explo/Exp_LeadIn_09.wav soundparms 0.8 0.2 0.7 0.5 900 16000 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
aliascache coop_arty_leadin_far4 sound/weapons/explo/Exp_LeadIn_11.wav soundparms 0.8 0.2 0.7 0.5 900 16000 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
aliascache coop_arty_leadin_far5 sound/weapons/explo/Exp_LeadIn_12.wav soundparms 0.8 0.2 0.7 0.5 900 16000 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
aliascache coop_arty_leadin_far6 sound/weapons/explo/Exp_LeadIn_13.wav soundparms 0.8 0.2 0.7 0.5 900 16000 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"

// ============================================================================================
// [user 2026-08-31] OMAHA CROWD BEDS - two 60-second walls of American voices that ship with the
// game and have never once been played.
//
// sound/dialogue/m3l1/A/amb_guys_rush.wav (60.1s) and amb_guys_shingle.wav (61.6s) are aliased in
// retail's uberdialog.scr as ambient_soldiers_runup / _shingle and referenced by no script in the
// game. They are hundreds of men shouting, ordering and screaming - the single biggest thing
// missing from a beach the user keeps saying is not chaotic enough.
//
// REDECLARED UNDER NEW NAMES, deliberately. Alias_ListAdd (qcommon/alias.c:322-328) keeps the
// FIRST definition and silently drops duplicates, and the retail aliases DO register here
// (their scope is maps "m dm obj", and "m" matches m3l1a). A same-name redeclare would lose.
//
// `loaded`, not retail's `streamed`: streamed sounds are rejected by S_OPENAL_Start3DLoopSound,
// so a streamed bed can never be a positioned loop. Both files are MONO, which is what lets them
// take the loaded path at all - S_LoadSound rejects non-mono non-streamed. Cost is ~5.4 MB
// resident for the pair, and bLoadForMap bounds it to m3l1a, so no other map pays it.
//
// 900/16000 rather than retail's 320/3000: the beach is roughly 6500 x 4000 units and a bed that
// pops in and out as you cross it is worse than no bed. Volume 0.65, not 1.3 - this sits UNDER
// everything and never stops, and values above 1 genuinely amplify in this build.
// ============================================================================================
aliascache coop_beachcrowd_rush sound/dialogue/m3l1/A/amb_guys_rush.wav soundparms 0.65 0.0 1.0 0.0 900 16000 auto loaded maps "m3l1a "
aliascache coop_beachcrowd_shingle sound/dialogue/m3l1/A/amb_guys_shingle.wav soundparms 0.65 0.0 1.0 0.0 900 16000 auto loaded maps "m3l1a "

//=========================================================================
//[user 2026-09-02, bug-2342] THE UNDERWATER SHOCK SEQUENCE.
//
//coop_underwater_wash is `local` - 2D, played straight to the client with playlocalsound - because
//it is what the player's own submerged ears hear, not a thing in the world with a position.
//
//The memory voices are the opposite: `auto` (3D) with a deliberately SHORT mindist of 140 and a
//long 2600 maxdist, so the same line is loud and close when its emitter spawns near the camera and
//a distant murmur when it spawns far. That is what makes them arrive from random directions and
//distances rather than all sitting in the middle of the head. The reverb, the low-pass and the
//slowing are baked into the samples - see docs/tools notes on the build - because reverb in this
//engine belongs to a trigger volume and there is no script command for it.
//
//Volume 1.0 with the samples themselves normalised to -24 LUFS: they must sit UNDER the underwater
//bed and the music, not compete with them.
//=========================================================================
//[user 2026-09-03] "underwater ambience could be a bit higher (the under water deep
//shellshock noise)". 1.0 -> 1.5, and the number only started meaning anything in the
//same change: coop_uwSay played this with playlocalsound, and Player::PlayLocalSound
//passes a hardcoded 1.0f to gi.Sound (player.cpp:18190) - the alias volume never left
//the server. The OPM_FEATURES branch above it that WOULD have sent alias->volume is
//dead code; OPM_FEATURES is not defined anywhere in this tree. So this alias said 1.0,
//coop_shellshock_uw said 1.7, and both played at exactly 1.0. coop_uwSay now uses
//`playsound`, which reaches Entity::Sound with argstype 0 (ProcessSoundEvent,
//entity.cpp:3405) and argstype 0 takes volume AND channel from the alias (:3751-3757).
//
//WHY 1.5 AND NOT MORE - the memory voices are the ceiling, not taste. They are played
//with `playsound` on a spawned emitter (coop_memoryVoices), so their 1.7 has always
//been real: 1.7 x their -24.72 dBFS sample = -20.11 alias-referred. This sample is
//-23.81, so 1.5 lands at -20.29 - a clear one-step lift that still leaves the voices
//just on top at closest approach and further under as they roll off past mindist 400.
//1.6 overtakes them; 2.0 swamps them, undoing the balance this file exists to keep.
//Peak-referred 1.5 x -9.67 dBFS = -6.15, no clipping (AL_MAX_GAIN is 8.0,
//snd_openal_new.cpp:837, so volumes above 1 genuinely amplify).
aliascache coop_underwater_wash sound/coop_tinnitus/coop_underwater01.wav soundparms 1.5 0.0 1.0 0.0 500 3000 local loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"

//[user 2026-09-04] THE BODY HITTING THE WATER. User-supplied recording (daviddumaisaudio,
//'large underwater explosion'), converted 48k stereo -> 22050 mono 16-bit and with the fade the
//user asked for BAKED IN over the last 2.11s of 6.60s. Measured peak per second after conversion:
//24794 / 15816 / 6564 / 3462 / 2352 / 759 / 40 - it decays to silence by itself, so nothing needs
//to stop it and it cannot outlive the beat.
//IN coop_tinnitus/ ON PURPOSE, like the surfacing gasp: the duck keys on the SAMPLE PATH
//(S_HZM_CueTier / S_HZM_DuckExempt in set_gain), this fires inside coop_rampAudioCut where
//s_sfxduck is 0.05, and coop_tinnitus/ is the one tier-1 path also carved out of coop_cueCut
//(bug-2373). On any unexempt path it would play at five percent and not be heard.
//1.3: the sample peaks at 24794/32767 = 0.757 full scale, so this lands at 0.98 - just inside.
//It sits over coop_underwater_wash (1.5) and the memory voices (1.7) and should be the loudest
//thing in the beat for its first second, which is what a body hitting water at speed sounds like.
//[2026-09-04 #2] CHANNEL `local` AGAIN, AND THE SUPERSEDED NOTE BELOW IS WRONG ON ITS CONCLUSION.
//`auto` did cure the steal - CHAN_AUTO is 0 and S_OPENAL_PickChannelBase's steal branch is gated on
//a NON-ZERO iEntChannel (snd_openal_new.cpp:1687), so a `local` sound can never evict it - but it
//moved this onto the 3D path, where three things go wrong at once:
//  1. THE ALIAS VOLUME IS DISCARDED. S_OPENAL_StartSound does set_gain(base * 1.3) at :2079 and
//     THEN calls set_3d() at :2083, whose last act is set_gain(S_GetBaseVolume()) at :4247 - with
//     no volume term. It overwrites the line above. The 2D path runs the same two calls in the
//     opposite order (set_no_3d :1959/:1963, set_gain(fRealVolume) :1967, play :1968), so 2D
//     honours the alias and 3D does not. Respatialize re-applies gain ONLY for channels
//     i >= MAX_SOUNDSYSTEM_CHANNELS_3D (:3264), so on 3D the wrong gain is frozen for all 6.60s.
//     The "1.3 x 0.757 = 0.98" arithmetic below never happened; it played at 0.757.
//  2. A 3D source sits at the PLAYER'S BODY (entity.cpp:3741 copies edict->s.origin), which is
//     still glued in the Higgins - measured 343 units BEHIND the cinematic camera at the landing
//     point - so the splash arrived from over your shoulder instead of around you.
//  3. For every non-host player it is then occlusion-traced through the boat hull (gain x0.55,
//     HF x0.12); occlusion is only skipped for the listener's OWN entity, snd_openal_new.cpp:3020.
//THE STEAL IS NOW AVOIDED BY THE EMITTER, NOT BY THE CHANNEL: this plays from
//$higgins1_playerspot, and coop_underwater_wash plays from $player[1], so the
//(iEntNum, iEntChannel) pair never matches and :1691-1697 cannot reach it. Nothing else plays
//`local` on $higgins1_playerspot (higgins_explosion is `weapon`, arty_exp_water is `weapon`,
//higgins_blowup_guys is `dialog`). If this ever moves back to a player entity, it must NOT be the
//same player entity the wash uses.
//--- superseded note, kept because its channel-steal analysis is still correct: ---
//[2026-09-04] CHANNEL `auto`, NOT `local`, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE REASON THIS IS AUDIBLE.
//coop_underwater_wash is played on the very next line, through the same coop_uwSay, so it resolves
//to the SAME player entity - and it also declares `local`. S_OPENAL_StartSound stops any channel
//whose iEntNum AND iEntChannel both match before starting the new one (snd_openal_new.cpp:1664),
//so as `local` this 6.60s impact was killed on the frame it started and had never once been heard.
//The wash stays on `local`: the surfacing gasp is MEANT to cut it that way, and that is documented
//at the BEAT 8 call site.
aliascache coop_uw_impact sound/coop_tinnitus/coop_uw_impact01.wav soundparms 1.3 0.0 1.0 0.0 500 3000 local loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"

//[user 2026-09-04] THE DROWNING MAN'S HEART. User-supplied recording; ONE lub-dub cycle cut out of
//it (1.370s..2.575s of the source = 1.205s, ~50bpm) and looped, rather than the whole 8.16s clip -
//the source is four beats that then STOP, and a stopping gesture repeated every eight seconds reads
//as a bug, not a heartbeat. Both cut points sit in the silent gap before a lub (levels 1192 and 213
//of 32767) with 5ms fades on top, so the loop has no seam.
//
//NORMALISED TO 0.85 FULL SCALE IN THE FILE, and that is not a stylistic choice. This is started with
//`playlocalsound <alias> 1`, and the loop branch of Player::PlayLocalSound sets
//edict->s.loopSoundVolume = 1.0f UNCONDITIONALLY (player.cpp:18186) - the alias volume below is read
//for the aliascache lookup and then thrown away. The only place the level can be set is the sample,
//so the sample carries it. Changing the 1.0 here will do nothing; re-normalise the wav instead.
//
//`loaded`, NOT `streamed`: S_OPENAL_AddLoopingSound early-returns on `!pSfx->length`, and a streamed
//sfx has no decoded length, so a streamed alias here is a silent no-op.
//minDist/maxDist are inherited from the DBNO heartbeat and are IGNORED - loopSoundFlags 1 is
//LOOPSOUND_FLAG_NO_PAN, which routes to the CHANNEL_FLAG_LOCAL_LISTENER branch (snd_openal_new.cpp
//:2508-2520): centred pan, no distance attenuation. It is 2D in the player's own head, by design.
aliascache coop_heartbeat sound/coop_heart/coop_heart01.wav soundparms 1.0 0.0 1.0 0.0 512 3000 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"

//[user 2026-09-04] "here is the audio for swimming, itll need to match the movement youve made."
//User-supplied recording, 46s of sparse underwater movement; ONE swoosh cut out of it - the one at
//12.10..12.88s, which is the most isolated in the file (peak 11007 against 21 before it and 102
//after, a 107:1 ratio) and within 11% of the loudest. 0.778s, so it fits inside a stroke with room:
//a stroke is ( 1.72 * coop_uwPace ) = 1.72s at pace 1.0 and 2.06s at the shipped 1.2.
//
//PITCH 0.94 + pitchMod 0.12 = 0.94..1.06 per play, because aliaspitch is
//`G_Random() * pitchMod + pitch` (entity.cpp:3337) and G_Random is 0..1. Six identical swooshes in
//twelve seconds read as a tape loop; a few percent of pitch each time reads as a body. This only
//works because it is played with `playsound` via coop_uwSay - playlocalsound resolves the alias and
//then discards both volume and pitch.
//
//CHANNEL `auto`, NOT `local`, and that is the whole reason it does not go through coop_uwJolt:
//CHAN_LOCAL is held for ~21s by coop_rampShellPanOne's shellshock wash, and six strokes landing on
//that channel would cut the wash six times. minDist 500 matches the other underwater aliases - the
//bodies sit ~200 units from the camera, so that is full volume.
aliascache coop_uw_swim sound/coop_swim/coop_uw_swim01.wav soundparms 1.0 0.0 0.94 0.12 500 3000 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"

//[user 2026-09-04] THE UNDERWATER BED - the ambience under the whole ramp-drop plunge, from the
//frame the body hits the water to the frame he breaks the surface. Started by
//maps/m3l1a/coopified.scr::coop_uwBedStart, stopped by coop_uwBedStop.
//
//sound/coop_swim/ IS LOAD-BEARING AND THE COUPLING IS INVISIBLE FROM HERE. coop_rampAudioCut holds
//s_sfxduck at 0.05 for this entire beat, and the ONLY thing that exempts this sample is the
//substring match on "coop_swim/" in S_HZM_DuckExempt (client/snd_openal_new.cpp, :3988 on
//2026-09-04). Move this wav to any other folder and the bed plays at FIVE PERCENT with no console
//error of any kind - the identical trap written up for coop_uw_break further down this file.
//coop_swim/ rather than coop_tinnitus/ on purpose: a tinnitus path is a TIER 1 CUE
//(S_HZM_CueTier), and a tier arms the sidechain, so a 26-second bed would hold the music and the
//flashback voices down for the whole sequence. Exempt from the duck, arming nothing.
//
//CHANNEL `local`, AND THAT IS THE ENTIRE REASON THE 1.8 BELOW MEANS ANYTHING. `local` is one of
//the two tokens that force the client 2D path (S_OPENAL_StartSound routes CHAN_MENU / CHAN_LOCAL /
//streamed / NO_OFFSET to S_OPENAL_Start2DSound), and that is the only path that carries the alias
//volume to AL_GAIN: Start2DSound calls set_no_3d() - which itself resets gain to the base - and
//THEN set_gain(fRealVolume) as the last write, and S_OPENAL_Respatialize re-applies it every frame
//for 2D channels. On `auto` the sound takes the 3D path, where set_3d() ends with
//set_gain(S_GetBaseVolume()) and the alias volume is simply gone - which is why coop_uw_swim's 1.0
//just above and coop_memvoice's 1.7 further down are NOT real numbers. (coop_uw_impact IS `local`,
//so ITS 1.3 is real - do not lump it in with those two.) `menu` would also reach 2D but set_gain
//skips the SFX slider for CHAN_MENU, so the player's Effects dial would not touch it.
//IT IS SAFE ON `local` ONLY BECAUSE IT IS PLAYED ON ITS OWN SPAWNED CARRIER ENTITY: on a player
//entnum it would steal CHAN_LOCAL from the wash and then be stolen by the surfacing gasp
//(S_OPENAL_PickChannelBase end_sample()s a live channel when iEntNum AND iEntChannel both match),
//which is bug-2436 exactly.
//
//dist 10000 / maxDist 12000 = LEVEL_WIDE_MIN_DIST (qcommon/q_shared.h:1585). The carrier sits 1200
//units up-beach purely so it is NOT on a player entity; the distance itself buys nothing on the
//CHANNEL_FLAG_LOCAL_LISTENER branch, where the pan is forced to dead centre by S_HZM_LocalPanAmount
//(it returns 0 for any sample whose name does not contain "coop_shellshock"). On the other branch
//the bearing pan applies and 1200 < dist 10000 gives full volume, so it is centred and loud either
//way. THE LOAD-BEARING PART OF THE PLACEMENT IS THE SEPARATE ENTITY, NOT THE DISTANCE.
//
//VOLUME 1.8 IS DERIVED, NOT PICKED, and it was re-derived on 2026-09-04 against the wav that
//actually ships. coop_uw_bed01.wav measures I = -23.9 LUFS integrated / -9.9 dBFS peak, so 1.8
//(+5.11 dB) puts it at -18.8 LUFS effective and -4.79 dBFS effective peak. Measured against the
//rest of this beat, all of which are `local` so their alias volumes are real: coop_underwater_wash
//-25.1 + 3.52 = -21.6, coop_shellshock_uw -23.5 + 4.61 = -18.9, coop_uw_break -16.5 + 1.58 = -14.9.
//So the bed sits 2.8 dB OVER the wash, level with the shellshock, and 4.1 dB UNDER the gasp that
//ends the beat - "up pretty high" without ever being the loudest thing. The 4.79 dB of remaining
//headroom is what bounds level.coop_uwBedVol to 1.5 in coop_uwBedStart. That headroom is measured
//at s_sfxvolume 1.0; CHAN_LOCAL follows the Effects slider (set_gain, 2026-08-07 change), and a
//player running it at 2.0 doubles this and everything else in the beat alike - coop_uw_break is
//already at -0.3 dBFS effective, so the bed is not the element that breaks first. If the wav is
//ever re-cut, re-derive: V = 10^((-18.9 - I_LUFS)/20), and check peak + 20*log10(V) <= -3.0 dBFS.
aliascache coop_uw_bed sound/coop_swim/coop_uw_bed01.wav soundparms 1.8 0.0 1.0 0.0 10000 12000 local loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"

//[user 2026-09-03] THE SURFACING BREATH. "when he comes out of the water use the
//existing breath exhale noise that we have from HOLDING SHIFT IN ADS to steady/hold
//breathe. That SPECIFIC breathe noise ... should be loud enough to hear."
//
//THE SAMPLE IS A BYTE COPY OF sound/coop_breath/breath_out.wav - literally the sound the
//user named. That file is played by PATH, never through an alias:
//  cgi.S_StartLocalSound("sound/coop_breath/breath_out.wav", qfalse)  cg_view.c:2221
//on the FALLING edge of the ADS breath-hold, whose trigger at :2205 is
//((bcmd.buttons & BUTTON_COOPADS) || bScoped) && bShift - ADS plus Shift, exactly as
//described. The original is untouched; this is a second copy under a different path.
//
//WHY A COPY AND NOT AN ALIAS ONTO coop_breath/, AND WHY NOT A CGAME HOOK. This lands
//inside coop_m3l1a_beachAudio's takeover: s_sfxduck 0.05 and coop_cueCut 0.30. The duck
//is applied in openal_channel::set_gain (snd_openal_new.cpp:3782-3812) and keys on the
//SAMPLE PATH - S_HZM_CueTier(pSfx->name) and S_HZM_DuckExempt(pSfx->name) - not on how
//the sound was started. "coop_breath/" is in NEITHER list, so anything under that path
//plays at five percent during this beat and cannot be heard. A cgame hook would not help:
//cgi.S_StartLocalSound routes CHAN_AUTO (cl_cgame.cpp:581), which is tier 0 and takes the
//same 0.05. Raising the alias volume cannot help either - punching through 0.05 needs x20
//and AL_MAX_GAIN is 8.0. "coop_tinnitus/" IS tier 1 (:3563) and is ALSO the one tier-1
//path carved out of coop_cueCut (:3855, added by bug-2373 so the concussion beat could not
//be pushed under the music), so sourced from here the gasp plays at 1.00. That is the
//whole reason for the copy, and it is why this needs no engine binary.
//S_HZM_DuckExempt is deliberately NOT touched: that list is global, and the narrower
//exemption this needs already exists.
//
//THE DIRECTORY NAME NOW LIES ABOUT THE CONTENTS - THIS COMMENT IS THE MITIGATION. If
//"coop_tinnitus/" is ever removed from S_HZM_CueTier, this gasp silently drops to 5% with
//no console error of any kind. The coupling is invisible from the script side.
//
//WHAT TIER 1 ALSO BUYS AND COSTS: multiplied by s_cueGain2 (archived, default 1), and it
//arms the cue sidechain for its length + 350ms - music and ambience x0.40, other SFX x0.91
//at the shipped s_cueDuck 2. The underwater bed is itself a tier-1 cue re-arming that same
//sidechain every frame, so the dip is already held at the break; this carries it about
//3.45s further, roughly 1.9s longer than the bed alone would have.
//
//VOLUME 1.2 IS MEASURED, NOT GUESSED, AND IS NOT THE PREVIOUS DRAFT'S 3.0. That number was
//calibrated for sound/coop_sprint/breath1.wav, which is a DIFFERENT sound (the >=5s sprint
//pant, player.cpp:16041) and 13.18 dB quieter. Measured, RMS of the loudest 400ms window:
//  breath_out.wav   peak -1.95 dBFS   loud400 -16.18 dBFS   3.10s
//  breath1.wav      peak -14.28 dBFS  loud400 -29.36 dBFS   4.12s
//3.0 on THIS sample is +9.54 dB and puts the peak at +7.59 dBFS - it clips right through
//the exhale. The target is level-continuity with the bed this cuts: coop_underwater01's
//-20.28 x 1.5 = -16.76 alias-referred, and breath_out at 1.0 is -16.18, already a clean
//handover. 1.2 adds 1.58 dB for the "loud enough to hear" and lands the peak at -0.37
//dBFS, just inside full scale. 1.25 is the HARD CEILING (peak exactly 0.0); above that the
//sample clips before any slider is involved. Tune inside 1.0 .. 1.25, never above.
//
//`local` (not the sprint aliases' `item`): CHAN_ITEM routes 3D - only CHAN_MENU and
//CHAN_LOCAL take the 2D path (snd_openal_new.cpp:1959-1962) - and 3D would place this at
//the player's body, glued and hidden in the boat, while the listener is out at the camera.
//CHAN_LOCAL also renders unattenuated pinned to each client's own listener (:1835), which
//is what makes one broadcast play land as one copy in every player's ears.
aliascache coop_uw_break sound/coop_tinnitus/coop_uwbreath01.wav soundparms 1.2 0.0 1.0 0.0 500 3000 local loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
//[user 2026-09-06, bug-2507] THE DROWNING MAN'S HEART, ONE BEAT AT A TIME (drowning_2026-09-06 3a(b)).
//The loop above cannot change rate (one loopSound int, player.cpp:18183), so the ramp fires this
//one-shot from script at an interval read off the air curve (1.10 s -> 0.50 s) on its own carrier.
//THE WAV IS ONE LUB-DUB SLICED OUT OF coop_heart01.wav (0.000..0.600 s of the loop cycle, 20 ms
//fade-out, 40 ms silent tail; 22050/16/mono like its source) and NORMALISED TO PEAK 0.68 FS so that
//the 1.4 here lands the peak at 0.95 FS - the loop is 0.85 FS at a hard-coded 1.0, so this is +1 dB
//over it. 1.47 IS THE CEILING (0.68 x 1.47 = 1.0); a playsound caller's volume arg replaces this
//number and must respect the same ceiling. sound/coop_heart/ is S_HZM_DuckExempt (snd_openal_new.cpp
//:4082, strstr "coop_heart/") and NOT in S_HZM_CueTier (:3968-3987), so it plays through the beat's
//s_sfxduck 0.05 and arms no sidechain - a beat every half second on a cue tier would pump the score.
//`local loaded` like coop_uw_break: 2D, no start gate, alias volume honoured on the local path.
aliascache coop_uw_heart sound/coop_heart/coop_uw_heart01.wav soundparms 1.4 0.0 1.0 0.0 500 3000 local loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
//[user 2026-09-06, bug-2507] THE FIRST BREATH - 0.9 s after the gasp (drowning_2026-09-06 3g).
//A BYTE COPY of sound/coop_breath/breath_in.wav (1.632 s, the ADS breath-hold inhale cg_view.c:2355
//plays by path). NOT aliased in place, for the reason coop_uw_break above is a copy: "coop_breath/" is
//in neither S_HZM_CueTier nor S_HZM_DuckExempt, and s_sfxduck is still 0.05 at the break - it is not
//restored until coop_m3l1a_beachAudio's rise ~100 s later (coopified.scr:9681, :12638) - so an alias on
//the original plays at five percent. It lives under sound/coop_swim/ rather than coop_tinnitus/: swim/
//is DuckExempt and NOT a cue tier (:4088), so it is heard and arms nothing, while the gasp one line
//above it is tier 1 and already holds the sidechain. Peak -5.89 dBFS x 1.2 = -4.3 dBFS, no clipping.
aliascache coop_uw_inhale sound/coop_swim/coop_uw_inhale01.wav soundparms 1.2 0.0 1.0 0.0 500 3000 local loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
//[2026-09-06, bug-2494 -> 2505] coop_uw_hitsand / coop_uw_strain are called by the plunge (coopified.scr
//coop_uwJolt, three sites) and are DELIBERATELY unaliased: the placeholders that sat here for six hours
//were played through playlocalsound on CHAN_LOCAL, which end-sampled the 14 s underwater wash bed at
//+2 s and again at stroke 1, and a sound/coop_tinnitus/ path is cue tier 1, so six strain jolts armed
//the music sidechain six times in ten seconds (drowning research 2026-09-06, section 2). When the user's
//real wavs arrive they go through coop_uwSay (playsound, its own channel), not the jolt. Until then the
//'needs to be aliased' line is the honest state.
aliascache coop_memvoice01 sound/coop_memory/coop_memvoice01.wav soundparms 1.7 0.05 1.0 0.05 400 2600 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
aliascache coop_memvoice02 sound/coop_memory/coop_memvoice02.wav soundparms 1.7 0.05 1.0 0.05 400 2600 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
aliascache coop_memvoice03 sound/coop_memory/coop_memvoice03.wav soundparms 1.7 0.05 1.0 0.05 400 2600 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
aliascache coop_memvoice04 sound/coop_memory/coop_memvoice04.wav soundparms 1.7 0.05 1.0 0.05 400 2600 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
aliascache coop_memvoice05 sound/coop_memory/coop_memvoice05.wav soundparms 1.7 0.05 1.0 0.05 400 2600 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"
aliascache coop_memvoice06 sound/coop_memory/coop_memvoice06.wav soundparms 1.7 0.05 1.0 0.05 400 2600 auto loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"

//=========================================================================
// HZM coop [user 2026-09-03] THE OMAHA RAMP SCREAMS.
//
// "if there is any death screams those should be played too before that explosion throws us
// overboard." Retail's five Higgins rangers (maps/m3l1a.scr::higgins1_disembark_kill) carry no voice
// call at all, so what they make today is the generic coop_deathvox grunt aihandler fires a frame
// after death - the coop layer having already muted their own native American cry. Driven by
// maps/m3l1a/coopified.scr::coop_rampScreams.
//
// SAME WAVS AS coop_av_us_wounded / coop_av_us_panic (ubersound/coop_aivoice.scr) - retail's generic
// AMERICAN pool. Confirmed American rather than assumed: sound/dialogue/Generic/{A,G,UK,US,it} splits
// by nationality, and models/human/animation/dialogue/Generic_dialogue_US.tik - the US dialogue set -
// is what fires dfr_death_* / dfr_damage_* off its death and pain anims (:99-203). G is German, it is
// Italian. Redeclared here rather than reused because this beat needs three things those pools cannot
// give it:
//
//   1. CHANNEL. coop_av_us_wounded and coop_av_us_panic are `dialog` (CHAN_DIALOG, 8), and
//      coop_mod/deathvox.scr::muteNativeVO stops channels 4, 7 and 8 on a dying man every frame for a
//      full second. A cry on any of those is silenced by our own mute a frame after it starts.
//      CHAN_ITEM (2) is chosen because nothing that can reach these five men inside this beat emits
//      on it - see the measured channel census in the coop_rampScreams header in coopified.scr, which
//      is where the reasoning lives. It is NOT because channel 2 is unused in the game: 910 aliases
//      in this very ubersound tree are declared `item`. Override and stopsound are both scoped to one
//      ENTITY (snd_openal_new.cpp:1664 and :2278), which is what makes the narrower claim enough.
//   2. LEVEL. 1.45 against the wounded pool's 1.15, and mindist 600 rather than 200, because these
//      five die inside an MG barrage with four to six snd_bh_flesh impacts going through each of
//      them; the beach casualties the wounded pool serves are heard in comparative quiet.
//   3. CACHE. `aliascache` precaches inside CG_RegisterSounds during CA_LOADING, behind the loading
//      screen, at zero configstrings - see coop_mod/sndcache.scr. `alias` (what both those pools use)
//      loads lazily at first play, a synchronous disk read in the middle of the one beat that must not
//      hitch. The marginal cost is NOT zero, contrary to an earlier draft of this note: those pools
//      are lazy, so these 33 files are genuinely new at load time - 991,154 bytes of PCM, measured,
//      against 2033 distinct paths already precached by this tree and a client ceiling of MAX_SFX
//      4096 (snd_local_new.h:181, a hard Com_Error; live count is cvar s_sfxCount).
//
// NAMES ARE ZERO PADDED. Alias lookup is a PREFIX match (Alias_ListFindRandomRange, qcommon/alias.c
// :553 - strncmp against the requested name's length), so an unpadded coop_rampdeath1 would also
// match coop_rampdeath10..14 and an explicit pick would not be the clip asked for. Two digits
// everywhere makes every name exact, while the bare pool names coop_rampdeath / coop_ramphit /
// coop_rampyell still pick evenly across their pools.
//
// DEATH CRIES - the 14 generic American death lines. Durations measured off the wav headers, and
// three of them are load-bearing: coop_rampScreamDeath pins 08 (2.543s) and 13 (1.419s) on the two
// men whose cries are cut off, so the cut is unmistakable, and pins 04 (0.407s) on ranger5 so his cry
// is over before coop_rampAudioCut ducks the world at T+3.72.
//=========================================================================
aliascache coop_rampdeath01 sound/dialogue/Generic/A/death/dfr_death_01a.wav soundparms 1.45 0.10 1.0 0.10 600 3000 item loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"	//0.691s
aliascache coop_rampdeath02 sound/dialogue/Generic/A/death/dfr_death_01b.wav soundparms 1.45 0.10 1.0 0.10 600 3000 item loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"	//1.161s
aliascache coop_rampdeath03 sound/dialogue/Generic/A/death/dfr_death_01c.wav soundparms 1.45 0.10 1.0 0.10 600 3000 item loaded maps "m e t dm obj train"	//0.874s
